// Urban craftsman workshop dwelling — timber-framed, shopfront on
// the street-facing gable. The bulk of Exeter's c.1300 housing
// stock per Kowaleski (1995) ch. 2: smaller-scale traders and
// craftsmen who didn't hold a full stone burgage. Open shopfront
// (CobbleRoad gap) is the period-typical shutter-down counter
// that doubled as a serving board during business hours.
